[Opening "Caro-Kann Defense: Karpov Variation"]

{Caro-Kann Defense: Karpov Variation. Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.}
1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nd7 5. Bd3 Ngf6 {Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.} 6. Ng5 e6 7. N1f3 h6 8. Nxe6 ! fxe6 {Prophylaxis. The move looks slow, and it takes away every active idea the opponent had.} (8... c5 Rb1 c4 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Bg6+ Ke7 10. Bf4 Qa5+ 11. c3 Qa6 ?! 12. Bc7 Nd5 13. Bg3 Kd8 14. Bd3 b5 15. a4 Qb7 16. O-O a6 17. Re1 N7f6 18. Bg6 Be7 19. Ne5 Rf8 20. Qf3 Ra7 21. b3 Bd6 22. axb5 cxb5 23. c4 Ne7 24. Be4 Qb8 25. Rad1 Bd7 26. c5 Bc7 27. b4 Kc8 28. Nxd7 Kxd7 29. d5 Bxg3 30. dxe6+ Kc8 31. hxg3 Rd8 32. Rd3 Rxd3 33. Qxd3 a5 34. Rd1 Qc7 35. Qxb5 a4 36. Qe2 a3 37. Bd3 Kb7 38. Bc4 Ra4 39. Rb1 Kb8 40. Ba2 Qc6 41. Qd2 Ra7 42. Qf4+ Qc7 43. Qd4 Ra4 44. Qd3 Qc6 45. Qd6+ Qc7 46. Qd3 Qc6 47. Qc3 Kc8 48. Qd2 Ned5 49. e7 Nxe7 50. Qd1 Ra7 51. b5 Qd7 52. Qe1 Kb8 53. Rd1 Qc8 54. Qe5+ Ka8 55. Qe3 Qe8 56. b6 Nc6 57. Bd5 Kb7 58. Bxc6+ Kxc6 59. bxa7 a2 60. a8=Q+ Qxa8 61. Rd6+ Kb5 62. Qd3+ Ka4 63. Rd4+ Ka5 64. Qa3+ Kb5 65. Qb4+ Kc6 {Resignation is timely: the king cannot be defended and the counterplay is one move too slow.} 66. Qb6# 1-0

