[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined: Orthodox Defense, Henneberger Variation"]

{Queen's Gambit Declined: Orthodox Defense, Henneberger Variation. Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.}
1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 d5 4. Bg5 Be7 5. e3 O-O {Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.} 6. Rc1 a6 7. Nf3 Nbd7 8. c5 ! c6 {A long think. Both continuations are playable; this one keeps more pieces on, which suits the attacker.} (8... a5 Ra1 a4 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. b4 b6 10. Bd3 a5 11. a3 axb4 ?! 12. axb4 Ba6 13. Bxa6 Rxa6 14. b5 cxb5 15. c6 b4 16. Nb1 Nc5 17. dxc5 bxc5 18. Bxf6 gxf6 19. e4 dxe4 20. Nfd2 f5 21. O-O Rxc6 22. Qh5 Bf6 23. Nc4 Qe7 24. Nbd2 Rcc8 25. f3 e3 26. Nxe3 Bd4 27. Nc4 Qf6 28. Kh1 Ra8 29. g4 fxg4 30. Nxg4 Qf4 31. Rc2 Kh8 32. Rg2 Rg8 33. Nce5 Rg7 34. Nc6 Bc3 35. Qxc5 Rag8 36. Rg3 f5 37. Nce5 fxg4 38. Nxg4 Qd4 39. Qb5 Rg5 40. Qe2 h5 41. Rh3 Qd5 42. Rd1 Qf5 43. Rd7 b3 44. Qb5 b2 45. Rd1 Rxg4 46. fxg4 Qxb5 47. Rxh5+ Qxh5 48. gxh5 Ra8 49. Kg2 Ra1 50. Rd8+ Kh7 51. Rd7+ Kh6 52. Rd6 b1=Q 53. Rxe6+ Kxh5 54. Re3 Qf1+ {The endgame is winning but not simple — the passed pawn needs its king, not just its rook.} 55. Kg3 1-0
